window.products.push({"id":582995,"name":"WGP Mosser Glass Hen Candy Dish, Vintage Style Covered Candy Bowl with Lid, 6 Inch, Jadeite Green Opaque Glass","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":38.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51uJHuqJX1L._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"Covered Hen Glass Dish: USA Made! Remember this little hen? Styled just like the hen on nest dishes of yesteryear, this gleaming glass version is handcrafted in our home state of Ohio! Beautifully made, it's the perfect size for filling with small candies. Just lift the \"hen\" lid and fill its \"nest.\" Hand-pressed by a family-owned and operated glassware company in Ohio. Available in different colors (each sold separately). Hand wash only. Dimensions: 6\"OD x 4-1/2\"H. USA made in Ohio. Crafted in Our Home State! This family-owned and -operated business makes some of the most beautiful glassware we've seen. Their classic designs and careful craftsmanship may just remind you of a different era. How It's Made Each piece is made following a time-honored method of pressing glass – from using cast iron molds to polishing and annealing (which the latter takes 3.5 hours alone). The results are stunning!How to Care for Your Mosser Glassware How you handle your glassware is important and will help protect it for years to come. Here are a few tips from Mosser Glass: Avoid glass to glass contact. If putting away your item on a shelf, avoid stacking.. Avoid quick changes in temperature. If it is cold from either being stored in a cool location or from just being washed, don't immediately fill it with hot liquids. Wait a moment until your Mosser Glass item is at room temperature before filling with a hot pot of coffee or tea. (Thermal shock happens from quick temperature changes - from hot to cold or cold to hot - causing your item to stress and crack or even break.). Avoid the misuse of the microwave. Do not heat or use glass containers for heating food packaged in heat concentrated materials (such as popcorn).. Don't add metal or tableware into glassware. Use plastic or nylon utensils to cook.. Clean with mild detergent and water. Let glassware reach room temperature before washing. Use nylon or plastic sponge to avoid scratches..","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51uJHuqJX1L._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Mosser Glass","source_asin":"B081B1PZCR","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-582995","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B081B1PZCR","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B081B1PZCR","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
